column2:
Apparently both sides of the face (seperated by the arete in the middle) has been skied!!! 

The line on the right side was climbed by Fred Touche and Drew Breyshaw, called &quot;A Beautiful Nightmare.&quot; 

Plinth peak is part of the Meager Complex, one of the volcanic vents. It's the highest of the cones. Mount Meager is left of centre.

Photographer: Afton Halloran
Title: &quot;Hemsedal Hills&quot;

This picture was taken as I was cross-country skiing alone in Hemsedal, South-Central Norway. It captures the mood of a lonely winter's day in Norway.

Photographer: Afton Halloran
Title: &quot;Songs of the Mountains&quot;
This photo was taken on the Tanzanian/Rwandan border. We were stuck for the night on the Tanzanian side as the sun set. After dark no one drives into Tanzania without an armed guard due to road bandits. My travel partner wanted some peace and quiet so he decided to play the guitar at the top of a hill. However, his white skin and strange instrument attracted a mass of children who came to sing and dance with us.

Photographer: Afton Halloran
Title of Photo: &quot;Champagne on the Rocks&quot;
Christian scrambles over the rocks on Chesterman's Beach, Tofino as the warm winter sun slowly sets.

Photographer: Afton Halloran
Title: &quot;Beginner's Luck&quot;
After setting out for a day long tour (and having barely any experience in x-country) in Hemsedal, Norway I fell in love with the sport.... and the landscape.

Photographer: Afton Halloran
Title: &quot;Bergen Fjord&quot;
After hiking around the hills behind the city of Bergen, Westcoast Norway the view from the top was the most rewarding moment of the whole day. Small island were dotted along the water, protecting the city from the harsh ocean.

Photographer: Afton Halloran
Title: &quot;1000 Eyes&quot;
The first sign of spring in Southern Norway.... the frog eggs are out!

I Call This One &quot;Big Mirror&quot;
Atlin Lake, BC
